n    <div class=\"seg3\"></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"main\">\n    <figure class=\"placeholder photo-col\" style=\"margin:0;\">\n      [Photo: surgeon in scrubs and mask in operating room, left column, full height]\n    </figure>\n\n    <div class=\"text-col\">\n\n      <div class=\"block\">\n        <div class=\"check\">&#10003;</div>\n        <div class=\"block-body\">\n          <h2>The Market Fundamentals</h2>\n          <p>The healthcare market is fundamentally different from any other commodity market. The fundamental difference is one cannot predict when demand will rise and fall. COVID-19 did away with all underlying presumptions about how the market behaves.</p>\n          <p>If patients are customers, the customers themselves cannot plan ahead on when to opt for healthcare services. ER/Accident distinguish this market in fundamental ways.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"spacer\"></div>\n\n      <div class=\"block\">\n        <div class=\"check\">&#10003;</div>\n        <div class=\"block-body\">\n          <h2>Healthcare Coverage Across the US</h2>\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0;\">Healthcare coverage has increased in America over the years due to the following reasons.</p>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Government-sponsored Medicaid plans</li>\n            <li>Medicare</li>\n            <li>Liberalization of laws</li>\n            <li>Competition amongst private health insurers</li>\n            <li>State-level health plans</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"chart-section\">\n    <div class=\"chart-head\">\n      <div class=\"check\">&#10003;</div>\n      <h2>Healthcare Coverage Stadistics</h2>\n    </div>\n\n    <p class=\"chart-label\">Adults Covered</p>\n\n    <div class=\"chart\">\n      <div class=\"bar-row\"><div class=\"bar bar-50\"></div><span class=\"bar-val\">50%</span></div>\n      <div class=\"bar-row\"><div class=\"bar bar-40\"></div><span class=